<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sigismund, Holy Roman Emperor</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1368–1437</span> · Also known as Sigismund of Luxembourg</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sigismund of Luxembourg was King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> from 1387, King of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> from 1411, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/king-of-bohemia">King of Bohemia</a> from 1419 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-emperor">Holy Roman Emperor</a> from 1433. He led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">crusade</a> defeated at Nicopolis in 1396 and convened the Council of Constance, which ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-schism">Western Schism</a> and condemned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jan-hus">Jan Hus</a>. He gave <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-hohenzollern">Hohenzollerns</a> in 1415, raised Savoy and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kleve">Cleves</a> to duchies and granted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> electorate to the Wettins in 1423.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sigismund-holy-roman-emperor.jpg" alt="Sigismund, Holy Roman Emperor" width="320" height="448" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Formerly attributed to Pisanello · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pisanello_024.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
